        "source": "valmikiramayan.net",
        "net_locator": "1-1-28, 1-1-29",
        "spans_beyond_this_verse": true,
        "translator": "K. M. K. Murthy / Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
        "text": "\"The citizens of Ayodhya and his father Dasaratha followed virtuous Rama for a distance when he started on his exile. Later Rama reached the tribal chief named Guha, who liked Rama, on the bank of River Ganga in a town called Sringaberapura. Together with Guha, Lakshmana and Seetha, he left off the charioteer. [1-1-28b, 29, 30a]"
      }
    ],
